# Sensing's menu contribution (#207): the Observe rows — what looking is available to $me.
#
# One row per (sensor, desired property): a sensor I poll, watching my subject, reporting a
# property I hold a desire in. The lever is the instrument; the direction column is empty
# because looking moves nothing, and that emptiness is data — a model reading the menu learns
# which moves change the world and which only change what I know.
#
# This branch lived in the deliberation package's menu.rq, which made the menu's KINDS a
# registry: adding a way of acting meant editing another package's file. It is sensing's walk
# — polls, monitors, observes are this package's own terms — so it ships from sensing's
# directory, and deleting this package deletes the rows, the terms and the executor together.
#
# `$me` is the one thing a shipped query cannot know, substituted by whoever collects the
# menu. Unqualified patterns on purpose: regions and wiring are public, so the row spans the
# default graph. Declares no prefixes of its own: `store.query` prepends them.

SELECT DISTINCT ?means ?property ?via ?direction ?mode WHERE {
  # An agent holds TWO shapes per property — the region it wants to be in and the survival
  # envelope it must not leave — and both carry `ssn:forProperty`, so matching on that alone
  # offered every lever twice. The severity is what tells them apart, and it is also the right
  # question: a lever is worth listing because there is something the agent WANTS about that
  # property, not because the property has an edge past which its subject dies.
  #
  # DISTINCT because a region carries three property shapes now — not looked, below, above —
  # and all three are wants. Matching a severity therefore matches three times per property,
  # and every lever would be offered three times. The row is about the property; which side
  # of it is unmet is the GOAL's business, not the menu's.
  # The properties this agent holds desires in arrive as $properties, asked of the DESIRE
  # MODALITY by the collector (a-store-is-a-modality, #298): the walk below is belief — wiring
  # and topology — and the shape patterns that used to sit here were the one desire-shaped
  # thing in it. An agent with no wants gets an empty VALUES and no rows, exactly as before.
  VALUES ?property { $properties }
  $me ag:actsFor ?subject .
  $me sensing:polls ?via .
  ?via sensing:monitors ?subject ;
       sosa:observes ?property .
  BIND(ag:Observe AS ?means)
  BIND(ag:Chosen AS ?mode)
}
